Fixed and verified.

**Bug:** `src/import_merge.ts:7` compared `b.url === inc.url` case-sensitively. Hostnames are case-insensitive, so `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` didn't match and got added as a second entry.

**Fix:** Normalize both URLs through `new URL(...).href` before comparing (case-normalizes the hostname, plus scheme/host); falls back to raw string comparison for non-URLs.

Verified: importing `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` against existing `https://example.com/a` now yields a single entry with unioned tags `["x","y"]`.


